\name{cellucid_highlight_cells}
\alias{cellucid_highlight_cells}
\title{Highlight cells}
\usage{
cellucid_highlight_cells(viewer, cells, color, label, page, tool = "annotation")
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{cells}{Cells: 1-based positions, \code{TRUE}/\code{FALSE} for every cell, or the cell names of the object the viewer shows, each once (sent as original positions). Required.}
\item{color}{The color of the page the group goes on. With \code{page}, the color of the page made (an existing page must already have it). Without, the page shown when it has this color, else the first page that has it, else a new page of it. Text. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{label}{The group's label; omitted, "Highlight" (the list shows its cell count). A label already on the page gets " (2)", " (3)", \ldots. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{page}{The page the group goes on, by name; a page of that name is made when there is none. Omitted: the page shown, or with \code{color}, a page of that color. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{tool}{The selection tool that made the cells (annotation for cells named directly). One of \code{"annotation"}, \code{"lasso"}, \code{"proximity"}, \code{"knn"}. Default \code{"annotation"}, the viewer's own.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Add a group of cells to a highlight page: a confirmed selection, or cells an agent or notebook names.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{highlight.cells} (Highlights). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{highlights}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_highlight_cells(viewer, cells = c(1,
      2, 3))
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
